One problem I see is that, in many cases, the argument of autoplot will be passed to fortify, to extract a data.frame from the object. And fortify has two arguments: model (the specialised object) and data (the original data). So in, that case, "model" would be the one you would want in autoplot. Calling it "data" will be confusing for fortify.

But I think using "model" might be a little to specific (not all autoplot arguments will be models). "object" looks like a better name to me.

Jean-Olivier Irisson
